using custom scripts, we calculated the window-averaged hydrophobicity score of each amino acid based on the Kyte-Doolittle method (the averaging of nince residues window for the central residue) and considered the continuous stretch of amino acids with a hydrophobicity score higher than 0.41 as the h-region. Based on the extracted h-region sequences, we then analyzed the properties, such as the hydrophobicity and length of the h-regions.
